{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on the skewness of the lotteries, specifically preferring the one that is more left-skewed (i.e., where favorable outcomes have higher probability relative to unfavorable ones). To assess skewness, we need to evaluate the distribution of outcomes relative to their desirability. In this context, less negative (or zero) outcomes are more favorable. Lottery A has a 50% chance of 0 Euros (favorable) and 50% chance of -1000 Euros (unfavorable), so the probability is evenly split between favorable and unfavorable outcomes. Lottery B has a 100% chance of -500 Euros, which is an unfavorable outcome but with certainty. Since Lottery A assigns 50% probability to a relatively favorable outcome (0 Euros) compared to the fully unfavorable B, Lottery A is more left-skewed. Thus, the decision reason would prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (outcomes and probabilities) is sufficient to compute skewness in a qualitative sense, so the reason can be applied.",
